 "summary": "Functoriality and cancellation of signed point twists are new to both Mathlib and Tau Ceti, and the PR reuses `bundleDiffeomorph`, `contMDiff_hom_bundle_iff`, `contMDiffAt_hom_bundle`, `ContinuousLinearMap.inCoordinates` and `contMDiff_bundleMap_of_constant_coordinates` wherever they apply. `VectorBundleCore.CoordinateHom` needs cores on both sides and does not apply to a general bundle `E`; building the cancellation diffeomorphism by hand is justified because `bundleDiffeomorph` requires finite rank.",
